WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.031 --> 00:00:04.992
The next morning Ally walked into town to shop for parts.

2
00:00:04.993 --> 00:00:08.191
It had taken only two hours to train Flo yesterday.

3
00:00:08.192 --> 00:00:14.674
The new waitress had learned the job so quickly, it was as if she'd been working at Ray's forever.

4
00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:17.915
As Ally walked along, she stopped and looked around.

5
00:00:17.916 --> 00:00:22.096
"I'm going to miss it here," she thought.

6
00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:27.464
"And I need to remember everything so I can tell my parents about Earth.

7
00:00:27.465 --> 00:00:33.619
After all, I am the first Astralian to make contact with Earthlings."

8
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:39.431
Ally began daydreaming about the elaborate welcome she'd receive when she returned home.

9
00:00:39.432 --> 00:00:42.998
"Mom and Dad will be so proud of me," she said.

10
00:00:42.999 --> 00:00:46.153
"I bet the elder council will give me a medal!"

11
00:00:46.154 --> 00:00:49.042
"A medal for what?" someone asked.

12
00:00:49.043 --> 00:00:53.214
Ally snapped out of her daydream to see Kate standing in front of her.

13
00:00:53.215 --> 00:01:00.728
"Oh, uh . . . nothing!" Ally said quickly.

14
00:01:00.729 --> 00:01:03.866
"I'd like to get a medal one day," Kate said.

15
00:01:03.867 --> 00:01:08.184
"Can you get one for having fantastic taste in fashion?"

16
00:01:08.185 --> 00:01:14.996
Ally laughed. "I don't know. But you deserve one!"

17
00:01:14.997 --> 00:01:18.362
"How come you're not working today?" Kate asked.

18
00:01:18.363 --> 00:01:23.454
"I have the morning off," Ally explained. "I have some shopping to do."

19
00:01:23.455 --> 00:01:28.924
"Ooh!" Kate said. "I'll come with you!"

20
00:01:28.925 --> 00:01:34.819
Ally gulped. She liked Kate a lot, but there was no way Kate could join this shopping expedition.

21
00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:41.548
"I'd really love that, but, um, I'm not shopping for anything exciting, just some, you know—"

22
00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:47.120
"Oh, boring things, like shampoo and soap?" Kate asked.

23
00:01:47.121 --> 00:01:49.533
"Exactly."

24
00:01:49.534 --> 00:01:54.901
"How about if we go shopping tomorrow after your work shift?" Kate asked.

25
00:01:54.902 --> 00:01:59.484
"I know the cutest dress shop! You'll love it. See you tomorrow!"

26
00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:03.104
Ally waved as she started toward the museum again.

27
00:02:03.105 --> 00:02:05.994
"Shopping with Kate sounds fun," she thought.

28
00:02:05.995 --> 00:02:08.382
"And I do have some extra money.

29
00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:13.845
I'd love to buy a new dress and wear it to my birthday party, when I finally get back home.

30
00:02:13.846 --> 00:02:21.355
I'll wow all my friends with unique Earth fashion!"

31
00:02:21.356 --> 00:02:27.594
The Sandville UFO Museum was a tall glass building with banners displaying planets and stars.

32
00:02:27.595 --> 00:02:31.837
As soon as Ally stepped through the door, an alarm blared.

33
00:02:31.838 --> 00:02:35.195
"Ahh!" She jumped back. "What did I do?"

34
00:02:35.196 --> 00:02:39.372
Phil, who worked as a security guard at the museum, hurried over.

35
00:02:39.373 --> 00:02:45.312
"These dang metal detectors!" He sighed and turned the alarm off.

36
00:02:45.313 --> 00:02:47.011
"You can come on in, Ally.

37
00:02:47.012 --> 00:02:52.201
We just installed these alarms for the sci-fi convention, and they go off at the littlest thing.

38
00:02:52.202 --> 00:02:54.443
I need to adjust them again."

39
00:02:54.444 --> 00:03:02.808
Phil held the door open for Ally, and she entered the main hall, which was filled with models of spaceships.

40
00:03:02.809 --> 00:03:06.148
"These silly things aren't usually here either," Phil said.

41
00:03:06.149 --> 00:03:10.211
"The convention organizers bring them in every year."

42
00:03:10.212 --> 00:03:15.339
Ally squinted at the models. She'd never seen ships like these before.

43
00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:19.025
"They're not very realistic."

44
00:03:19.026 --> 00:03:22.312
"You're telling me." Phil rolled his eyes.

45
00:03:22.313 --> 00:03:27.901
"Well, enjoy the museum. I need to fix these alarms."

46
00:03:27.902 --> 00:03:32.819
Ally was tempted to look around at some of the exhibits, but she reminded herself that she didn't have much time.

47
00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.783
She had to get the parts and then get to the diner for work by noon.

48
00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:41.814
She hurried into the gift shop and found a sales clerk.

49
00:03:41.815 --> 00:03:49.208
"Excuse me. Can you tell me where I can find fuel cells, beta-booster coils, and other spaceship parts?"

50
00:03:49.209 --> 00:03:52.178
"Ha-ha," the clerk said.

51
00:03:52.179 --> 00:03:55.484
Ally frowned. "What's so funny?"

52
00:03:55.485 --> 00:03:58.975
"Listen, kid, the convention hasn't started yet.

53
00:03:58.976 --> 00:04:03.566
Until it does, spare me the wacko sci-fi talk, okay?"

54
00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:07.548
"But I really need these parts," Ally said.

55
00:04:07.549 --> 00:04:09.896
"I'm sure you do," the clerk said.

56
00:04:09.897 --> 00:04:14.009
"But like I've told a million other people, we don't sell that kind of stuff here.

57
00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:17.869
You should go to Everything Mart, like everyone else."

58
00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:22.864
"Thanks," Ally said. She turned around, trying to decide what to do.

59
00:04:22.865 --> 00:04:27.984
Going to Everything Mart seemed like the only option; she didn't have any other ideas about where to shop.

60
00:04:27.985 --> 00:04:32.689
"I still have plenty of time," she thought. "As long as—"

61
00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:37.819
"Ally!" Dr. Lloyd hurried over. "I'm glad I ran into you!

62
00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:43.208
I want to invite you to the opening of my exhibit on Friday, the first day of the convention."

63
00:04:43.209 --> 00:04:48.997
"I'd love to come," Ally said politely, even though she knew she'd be zooming through outer space by then.

64
00:04:48.998 --> 00:04:52.469
"It's going to be so exciting," Dr. Lloyd said.

65
00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:58.250
"I'll be unveiling proof that extraterrestrial life-forms not only exist, but also . . ."

66
00:04:58.251 --> 00:05:02.165
He paused to look around before leaning in close to her.

67
00:05:02.166 --> 00:05:05.968
"They are here among us—closer than anyone thinks.

68
00:05:05.969 --> 00:05:10.881
And we have to be prepared to fight them off!"

